  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Recent changes in the W3C WebACL ontology have defined acl:agentGroup as the predicate to use for group access with the range of vcard:Group.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "For more information, see the ontology (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl)"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and the archived discussion that resulted in the addition of the predicate (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-rww/2016Jan/0024.html)"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-rww/2016Jan/0024.html)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Based on some discussions in the Hydra slack channel with ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "6089a48d248ef60073948d92",
        "text": "@Unknown"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65",
        "text": "@Esmé Cowles"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "5fca8b70dd0c5900755cbefb",
        "text": "@matienzo"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": ", Fedora should adopt this predicate for group permissions to keep current with the ontology. Because acl:agentClass is presently used, ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "6089a48d248ef60073948d92",
        "text": "@Unknown"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " suggested Fedora should support both and remove the former after such a time that the ontology is officially published or that tooling is available to migrate any existing predicates to their new values.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
